<title>ITALY: Fiat says share of Bahrain order worth 250bln lire.</title>
<headline>Fiat says share of Bahrain order worth 250bln lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fisia Italimpianti, the engineering and contracting unit of Fiatimpresit, said its share of a turnkey order for a desalination plant in Bahrain was worth 250 billion lire.</p>
<p>Fisia Italimpianti is part of a consortium led by electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG which won a $458 million contract to build a gas-fired power and desalination plant at Hidd on the Muharraq Island in Bahrain.</p>
<p>Fiatimpresit is part of Italian industrial group Fiat. (( --Milan bureau +392 66129507))</p>
</text>
